From 974ae92cd27230ba998c9071fbc8e5051b0cf4d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sarvsaur <quic_sarvsaur@quicinc.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Feb 2025 14:58:33 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] Initiate codec negotiation when AT+BCC is received

As per HFP specification, codec negotiation
is needed once after SLC if both sides support
it. For suesequent SCO connections, codec negotiation
is not needed. However, some remotes sending
AT+BCC and expecting codec negotiation though
codec on headset has not changed from previous
SCO connection.

With this CL, AG initiates codec negotiation
when AT+BCC is received from remote.

Bug: 397138373
Change-Id: I2ef85cfed601600b50612c18d546fb6f17abfbce
Signed-off-by: Pranav Temkar <pranavtemkar@gmail.com>
---
 system/bta/ag/bta_ag_cmd.cc | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/system/bta/ag/bta_ag_cmd.cc b/system/bta/ag/bta_ag_cmd.cc
index d939006c36..5a812d1904 100644
--- a/system/bta/ag/bta_ag_cmd.cc
+++ b/system/bta/ag/bta_ag_cmd.cc
@@ -1379,6 +1379,8 @@ void bta_ag_at_hfp_cback(tBTA_AG_SCB* p_scb, uint16_t cmd, uint8_t arg_type, cha
       }
 
       bta_ag_send_ok(p_scb);
+      log::info("Initiating codec negotiation");
+      p_scb->codec_updated = true;
       bta_ag_sco_open(p_scb, tBTA_AG_DATA::kEmpty);
       break;
     }
-- 
